1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,700
There is a game called How to Fish.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,360
A boat. A rod. A lot of fish.

3
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:08,860
And almost nobody seems to be fishing.

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:11,258
They are slapping each other in the face.

5
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:13,120
It costs about eight dollars.

6
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:15,050
A message in a group chat.

7
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:17,089
"It's eight dollars. Just get it."

8
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:19,920
Bought. Bought. Bought.

9
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:23,083
And one friend who says
"I'll get it later."

10
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:25,480
He will not get it later.

11
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,720
Getting a few adults into the same boat

12
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:30,770
is harder than anything
in the game. And yet,

13
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:34,160
millions of people bought a fishing game.

14
00:00:34,390 --> 00:00:37,160
To do everything else. Together.

15
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:39,100
So, why?

16
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:45,595
Start with the price. Eight dollars is
not really a price. It's an invitation.

17
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:49,366
Its makers hoped it might sell
two hundred thousand copies.

18
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:54,480
By early October, one analytics firm
estimated more than ten million.

19
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:58,040
Because this is not really
a game you play alone.

20
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:01,060
Everyone in the boat buys their own copy.

21
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:05,590
Now compare that with the other way
adults try to see their friends.

22
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:06,900
"We should hang out."

23
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:08,220
"Yes! Definitely."

24
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:09,930
"I'm free in three weeks."

25
00:01:09,970 --> 00:01:11,260
"Three weeks works."

26
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:14,300
And three weeks later,
somebody's kid is sick.

27
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:16,609
Somebody's car is making a new noise.

28
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:21,560
And the plan quietly dies in a chat
nobody will ever scroll back to.

29
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,686
As an adult, the hard part of
seeing your friends is not distance.

30
00:01:25,730 --> 00:01:28,500
It isn't even time. It's asking.

31
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:32,080
Proposing a plan means
admitting you want one.

32
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:33,960
Kids never had this problem.

33
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,367
A kid just shows up at your
door and says: "Want to play?"

34
00:01:37,630 --> 00:01:40,280
At some point, we lost that sentence.

35
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,844
Nobody ever told us what replaced it.

36
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:45,100
Eight dollars removes the asking.

37
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:49,380
But why fishing? Of all the
things a game could be about.

38
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:52,310
Because fishing solves a second problem.

39
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:53,560
Not how to meet.

40
00:01:53,750 --> 00:01:55,990
What to do once you're there.

41
00:01:56,190 --> 00:01:59,450
Ask anyone what they caught
on their last fishing trip.

42
00:01:59,490 --> 00:02:02,896
Most don't remember. They
remember who was in the boat.

43
00:02:02,990 --> 00:02:07,798
In a boat, nobody has to look at each
other. Nobody has to fill the silence.

44
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:09,699
You both look at the water.

45
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:13,610
You talk. Or you don't,
and that is fine too.

46
00:02:13,650 --> 00:02:16,630
The fish gives the afternoon a reason...

47
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,820
and the silence a job.

48
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:22,656
And fishing is not the only
alibi adults have invented.

49
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:25,010
The golf course. The poker night.

50
00:02:25,150 --> 00:02:28,390
The car that needs one more
afternoon in the garage.

51
00:02:28,610 --> 00:02:33,650
Nobody in those places is really there
for the golf, the cards or the car.

52
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:37,950
Every generation has built its own
excuse to sit next to each other.

53
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:40,630
How to Fish is just the newest one.

54
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,550
It fits in a group chat.

55
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:46,290
And like every good alibi,
it comes with props.

56
00:02:46,810 --> 00:02:49,770
A boat. A rod. A goal.

57
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:52,460
And then it gets rid of
it almost immediately.

58
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,610
You begin with almost nothing.

59
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:57,590
Soon you have guns and dynamite.

60
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,100
You sell your catch.

61
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:01,670
You gamble the money. You fight bosses.

62
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:03,950
The developers' own description on Steam

63
00:03:03,990 --> 00:03:05,730
reads, word for word:

64
00:03:06,110 --> 00:03:10,830
"cartoon violence towards fish and
gambling with fish (no real money)."

65
00:03:10,870 --> 00:03:12,610
The goal is still there.

66
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:14,690
But the goal is not the point.

67
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:16,490
The goal is the alibi.

68
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:20,470
And what happens instead of
fishing... is mostly failure.

69
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:22,430
Someone falls in the water.

70
00:03:22,470 --> 00:03:26,070
Someone finds a weapon that was
clearly not designed for fish.

71
00:03:26,110 --> 00:03:27,933
Someone gambles the savings,

72
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:30,570
and nobody will ever admit who it was.

73
00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:32,650
Someone gets launched across the island

74
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:35,696
by something they absolutely
should not have poked.

75
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:40,110
And when a teammate goes down, the way you
bring them back is by picking them up...

76
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:42,350
and slapping them in the face.

77
00:03:42,710 --> 00:03:46,290
Which, if we're honest, is how
most friendships handle feelings.

78
00:03:46,330 --> 00:03:49,176
Nobody retells the time
everything went perfectly.

79
00:03:49,290 --> 00:03:51,990
They retell the night it all went wrong.

80
00:03:52,350 --> 00:03:55,930
Usually years later, in the same
group chat, with no context,

81
00:03:55,970 --> 00:03:58,610
to the confusion of
everyone who wasn't there.

82
00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:03,220
The internet even invented a name
for games like this. Friendslop.

83
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:05,147
Half a joke, half an insult.

84
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:08,640
Cheap, chaotic co-op games
built for playing with friends.

85
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:12,140
We named a whole genre
after the word for garbage.

86
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:14,799
Then we invited our friends to it.

87
00:04:14,850 --> 00:04:16,310
Some say it's short.

88
00:04:16,350 --> 00:04:18,665
Maybe it is just this year's summer hit.

89
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:21,153
But fishing trips end too.

90
00:04:21,410 --> 00:04:23,398
That was never what they were for.

91
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:26,520
Some games just need to get a
few friends into the same boat

92
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:29,460
on a Tuesday night. The plan was to fish.

93
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:32,080
The plan is always to fish.

94
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:36,577
And at some point, around one in the
morning, someone says "last round."

95
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:38,820
It is never the last round.

96
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:41,700
And the two friends who
founded the studio behind it?

97
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:45,830
They met in high school. Their
first paid game had not done well.

98
00:04:45,870 --> 00:04:49,630
So they made a small game about
friends doing something silly together.

99
00:04:49,670 --> 00:04:53,220
And millions of people
answered the same group chat.

100
00:04:53,950 --> 00:04:58,820
So... why did millions of people
buy a fishing game and not fish?

101
00:04:59,270 --> 00:05:02,180
Because nobody in that
boat came for the fish.

102
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:05,400
The fish was just the thing
you could say out loud.

103
00:05:05,790 --> 00:05:09,740
How to Fish sounds like a
tutorial. And maybe it is.

104
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:11,300
Just not for fishing.

105
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,980
It teaches the thing adults are worst at.

106
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,850
How to say "I miss you"...

107
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,840
without ever having to say it.

108
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:20,177
So who would you put in your boat?

109
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:22,640
And what game deserves a "why?" next?

110
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:24,228
Tell me in the comments.

111
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,469
Maybe that's our next quest.
